// C416(n): a finding at node n, from clause `list-comprehension`.
// Each rule below is one way the JSON `rule` can match.
// Columns after `at` are the metavariables the JSON's message, anchor or `each` names: one finding per distinct row.
// The JSON `transform` computes KN from other metavariables' text; its literals end each rule.
.violation C416(at: loc, c416_comp: node, it: loc) "Replace this comprehension with `list({it})`, which copies the same items; keep it inside `__len__`, where `list()` can recurse."
    suppress noqa "C416"
C416(COMP, n, IT) :- node(_, n, _, _, _), W = n, c416_alt_17(n, COMP, IT, KN, _, _, W), text(W, t1),
    KN = @replace_all(t1, "(?s)^.*$", "list").

// C416_set_comprehension(n): a finding at node n, from clause `set-comprehension`.
